      {
        "id": 233672,
        "name": "Martin Tenbones",
        "username": "Martin_Tenbones",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/e5b9ba/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-15T15:10:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I mean, I can definitely see how mechanically strong Fangs and Minds make each other with a smooth mix of offense, defense, mobility, and much easier access to non-Jungle lands for Fangs, but I still feel something is missing without Trickster.&nbsp; Fangs and Minds working together, Invaders are all like, \"And then our supply lines were ambushed from both sides simultaneously by packs of tigers.&nbsp; We left the men to fight while the officers retreated in order not to miss tea, we're still waiting to hear back from them.&nbsp; I say, were tigers always pack hunters and we just didn't realize it?\"&nbsp; But adding Trickster in, it's \"Well, no, I don't think they were pack hunters when we were on campaign in India... wait, who is that at the door?&nbsp; Grandma?&nbsp; Is that you?&nbsp; Why, you've come all the way from England on holiday to visit me, what a lovely surprise!&nbsp; But what big eyes you have, and what big teeth, and wha... oh dear God, no!!!\"</p>\n<p>Moral: It's the *unexpected* tigers that'll get ya.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:09:33.853Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
