        "raw": "<p>I mean, I can definitely see how mechanically strong Fangs and Minds make each other with a smooth mix of offense, defense, mobility, and much easier access to non-Jungle lands for Fangs, but I still feel something is missing without Trickster.&nbsp; Fangs and Minds working together, Invaders are all like, \"And then our supply lines were ambushed from both sides simultaneously by packs of tigers.&nbsp; We left the men to fight while the officers retreated in order not to miss tea, we're still waiting to hear back from them.&nbsp; I say, were tigers always pack hunters and we just didn't realize it?\"&nbsp; But adding Trickster in, it's \"Well, no, I don't think they were pack hunters when we were on campaign in India... wait, who is that at the door?&nbsp; Grandma?&nbsp; Is that you?&nbsp; Why, you've come all the way from England on holiday to visit me, what a lovely surprise!&nbsp; But what big eyes you have, and what big teeth, and wha... oh dear God, no!!!\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Moral: It's the *unexpected* tigers that'll get ya.</p>",
